<title>UK: United News plans cable TV giant -paper.</title>
<headline>United News plans cable TV giant -paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>United News &amp; Media Plc is considering a move into cable television as part of a plan to create a 1 billion stg ($1.6 billion) rival to Cable and Wireless Communications Plc, the Sunday Times said.</p>
<p>Under the plan, United would take a big minority stake in a cable company created by the merger of Telewest Communications Plc and NTL Inc.</p>
<p>The paper said the plan could create much needed consolidation in the cable industry.</p>
<p>No-one at United News could be reached for comment.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom + 44 171 542 7717 ($ = 0.612 British Pounds)</p>
